nent":"LA","home":false,"pf":37.0,"pa":34.0,"off_snaps":58,"epa_per_play":0.2914,"pass_rate":0.3621,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4043,"def_epa_per_play":0.2306},{"week":6,"opponent":"LV","home":false,"pf":33.0,"pa":30.0,"off_snaps":61,"epa_per_play":0.171,"pass_rate":0.5738,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5962,"def_epa_per_play":0.09507}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"CHI","distance":0.5212,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2022,"team":"DET","distance":0.5639,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.5927,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2024,"team":"DET","distance":0.6633,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2022,"team":"LA","distance":0.6808,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Sean McVay"}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.4102,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"MIA","distance":0.4902,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"PIT","distance":0.5084,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.5482,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"DET","distance":0.5528,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Bills are 5-1 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 197 to 171. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 1st in EPA per play while the defense sits 29th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits are the lowest shotgun rate and the 3rd highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Bills have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in all five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the lowest shotgun rate and the highest under center rate in the league. Josh Allen has run the passing game, with Khalil Shakir leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Bills have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 26th or worse in four of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, takeaways per game, only ranks 16th, and it is 29th in EPA allowed per dropback. Gregory Rousseau has led the way with 6 sacks. In terms of scheme, they have the 3rd highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Bills have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 60% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 100% of field goals, which is the best in the league. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their secondary was among the youngest in the league.","players":"Josh Allen has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,504 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Khalil Shakir and Dalton Kincaid leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. James Cook has handled most of the work in the backfield with 91% of the carries. On defense, Gregory Rousseau leads the team with 6 sacks.","coaching":"Joe Brady is calling the offense as head coach and Jim Leonhard is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Bears and the 2022 Lions, both under Ben Johnson. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Jets and the 2025 Dolphins.","trends":"The offense went from 3rd in EPA per play in 2025 to 1st so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 13th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 29th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was eight man box rate, which went from 5% to 14%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}